AI Usage Log Entry 4
Task ID/Title: Coordinate Sequential Pull Request Merging
Purpose of AI Use:
Project planning and Git workflow guidance. AI was used to determine an appropriate step-by-step Git workflow for reviewing and merging two team members' feature branches into the main branch sequentially. The goal was to coordinate the Registration UI and Login UI Pull Requests while reducing the risk of merge conflicts.
Chat Link or Prompt/Response:
Prompt:
"My team member Dany and I both have open PRs (Registration UI and Login UI) targeting main. What is the best step-by-step Git workflow for us to review and merge our branches into main sequentially without causing merge conflicts?"
AI Response:
The AI recommended coordinating the Pull Requests and merging them sequentially rather than merging both at the same time. The suggested workflow included reviewing the first Pull Request, merging it into main, updating the second feature branch with the latest changes from main, resolving and testing any conflicts if they occurred, and then reviewing and merging the second Pull Request.
The AI also explained that keeping feature branches synchronized with main and communicating with the other team member can reduce the likelihood of conflicts.
AI-Suggested Content:
The AI suggested the following general workflow:
1.	Decide which Pull Request will be reviewed and merged first.
2.	Review the first Pull Request and check that its changes are ready.
3.	Merge the first Pull Request into main.
4.	Update the second feature branch with the latest version of main.
5.	Resolve any merge conflicts if they occur.
6.	Test the updated second branch to make sure the changes still work.
7.	Request/review the second Pull Request.
8.	Merge the second Pull Request into main after approval and successful checks.
9.	Communicate with the team throughout the process to avoid both members making conflicting changes at the same time.
Validation:
The suggested workflow was reviewed against the team's GitHub branching and Pull Request process. The team also considered which branches contained overlapping changes and used GitHub Pull Requests to review the changes before merging. The workflow was applied to the Registration UI and Login UI branches, and the branches were checked after merging to make sure the project continued to build and function correctly.
Decision:
Modified before use. The general workflow was accepted, but the exact sequence and steps were adjusted based on the team's branch structure, Pull Request status, and review process.
Reflection:
The AI assistance helped clarify how two team members could coordinate Pull Requests targeting the same main branch. It reinforced the importance of reviewing and merging changes sequentially, keeping feature branches updated, and communicating with teammates. The interaction also helped us understand that conflicts cannot always be completely prevented, but they can be reduced and handled systematically.
